bibliograph-web (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.0 release: feed generator, admin curation and split packaging.

    - Serve com.atproto.feed.describeFeedGenerator and getFeedSkeleton at the
      edge from HappyView's activity index; personalized feeds require
      FEED_GENERATOR_DID and PLC_URL.
    - Expand the private /admin UI with publisher search, book preview and
      bounded bulk import proxied to the worker admin API.
    - Show live catalog statistics and cap anonymous hydration enqueues.
    - Read publisher records through PDS_URL and serve the books-wg catalog
      procedures from the read-only catalog DATABASE_URL.
    - Ship the TLS vhost as a conffile and enable it only when a certificate
      and a valid nginx configuration make that safe.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-web (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. The SvelteKit edge from packages/web, built with
    adapter-node and running on the host's nodejs:

    - bibliograph-web.service serves the UI and /xrpc on 127.0.0.1:5176.
    - The proxy injects the configured HappyView XRPC client identity and
      relays Authorization/DPoP untouched; it holds no user session.
    - /etc/bibliograph/web.env carries the upstream URL and the client
      key/secret.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +0000
